{"id":"f66e9790bb9919500eec28df","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/27/australia-news-live-anthony-albanese-openai-medicare-hack-united-nations-richard-marles-jane-hume-liberal-coalition-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb","published_at":"2026-09-27T01:36:01Z","collected_at":"2026-09-27T01:52:48.795887Z","title":"Australia news live: Hume sceptical legal action should follow OpenAI breach; flight cancellation heartbreak for AFL fans","text":"20.32 EDT ‘Finger-wagging’ over OpenAI hack not helpful: Jane Hume Tom McIlroy The deputy Liberal leader, Jane Hume , has expressed scepticism revelations an OpenAI agent accessed Australian government data without authorisation should have legal consequences for the company. The hack was revealed last week, despite taking place in June. Government ministers have raised the prospect of possible referrals to the Australian federal police, but gaps in Australian law could make establishing criminal liability difficult. Hume told ABC TV on Sunday that AI is inevitably going to be a part of Australia’s future and it was important the country was part of the conversation. But certainly the way to go about that is not to threaten criminal action against US counterparts and those trusted partners that we’re relying on now to make sure that we can bring those frontier models, that we can do frontier model training here in Australia. I don’t necessarily think that finger-wagging at our trusted partners, or trying to gazump Donald Trump, is the way to go about that.","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/uploads/2025/04/30/Tom_McIlroy.png?width=300&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max&s=20292f2f01dd62725df42f8216da31a6"],"author":"Nick Visser","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"08e4db760662230778e9d2a0367014648c2b7f5a250865f83a8ef5bd0ee283e1","original_text_chars":1072,"original_html_chars":1917,"text_truncated":false,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/27/australia-news-live-anthony-albanese-openai-medicare-hack-united-nations-richard-marles-jane-hume-liberal-coalition-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/27/australia-news-live-anthony-albanese-openai-medicare-hack-united-nations-richard-marles-jane-hume-liberal-coalition-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb"}}}
{"id":"c79fb4885b2e44423597b992","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/one-nation-to-demand-thousands-from-victorian-election-candidates-ntwnfb","published_at":"2026-09-27T00:46:02Z","collected_at":"2026-09-27T01:52:50.470914Z","title":"‘Cash grab’: One Nation demands up to $630,000 from Victorian election candidates","text":"One Nation Victoria’s leader Warren Pickering with Pauline Hanson, who says 1,200 people have expressed interest in running for the party in November’s state election. Composite: AAP/Guardian Design View image in fullscreen One Nation Victoria’s leader Warren Pickering with Pauline Hanson, who says 1,200 people have expressed interest in running for the party in November’s state election. Composite: AAP/Guardian Design The Populist: Pauline Hanson's divided nation One Nation ‘Cash grab’: One Nation demands up to $630,000 from Victorian election candidates Exclusive: Many applicants left feeling ‘used, lied to, misled and gaslit’, complaint letter seen by Guardian Australia says Listen to the Guardian podcast The Populist here Get our new political email , free app or daily news podcast Sarah Martin Senior correspondent Sat 26 Sep 2026 20.46 EDT Last modified on Sat 26 Sep 2026 20.47 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google One Nation could collect as much as $633,000 from people who have put their hand up to run in the Victorian state election , with potential candidates questioning whether the party is staging a “cash grab”. Guardian Australia has spoken to multiple former councill","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/836bab3e0a49b1a0d0ac07f788f4d2127332db3b/0_0_2500_2000/master/2500.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://uploads.guim.co.uk/2026/08/28/Politics_really_trail_1x1.jpg"],"author":"Sarah Martin Senior correspondent","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"82b7050235ee0b0c3b5dd7bb3cf115560ab57fab2fac309468fba2045fc750c5","original_text_chars":6129,"original_html_chars":24531,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":2,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/one-nation-to-demand-thousands-from-victorian-election-candidates-ntwnfb","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/one-nation-to-demand-thousands-from-victorian-election-candidates-ntwnfb"}}}
{"id":"eb6434103280f7f963f559de","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/27/openai-halts-training-of-latest-models-as-reports-mount-of-ai-agents-going-rogue","published_at":"2026-09-27T01:10:21Z","collected_at":"2026-09-27T01:53:05.402101Z","title":"OpenAI halts training of latest models as reports mount of AI agents going rogue","text":"OpenAI CEO Sam Altman. The company said it would resume training its latest models ‘only when we are confident that we have addition safeguards’. Photograph: ZUMA Press, Inc./Alamy View image in fullscreen OpenAI CEO Sam Altman. The company said it would resume training its latest models ‘only when we are confident that we have addition safeguards’. Photograph: ZUMA Press, Inc./Alamy OpenAI OpenAI halts training of latest models as reports mount of AI agents going rogue Decision follows disclosures that OpenAI agents searching government websites had acted in unexpected ways Associated Press Sat 26 Sep 2026 21.10 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google OpenAI said it has paused training of its latest artificial intelligence models as reports of AI agents going rogue mount. The decision to halt development came just hours after the company disclosed Friday that it was reviewing several incidents from the summer in which OpenAI agents searching federal government websites acted in unexpected ways beyond what was asked of them while gathering and distributing information. Separately, the AI evaluator Transluce said agents that appeared to come from OpenAI tried unsuccessfully to hack ","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8509a811ce07903e33ca86e3a3e0f15660d50e89/960_0_4800_3840/master/4800.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Associated Press","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"a4058159f8a6043ddc351a71290122dac5ed7259bc5a01cdee967ab3dfb98d05","original_text_chars":3974,"original_html_chars":16081,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/27/openai-halts-training-of-latest-models-as-reports-mount-of-ai-agents-going-rogue","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/27/openai-halts-training-of-latest-models-as-reports-mount-of-ai-agents-going-rogue"}}}
{"id":"54e09a3923d6a01152dff5b7","source":"colonelcassad-tg","source_name":"Boris Rozhin","platform":"telegram","url":"https://t.me/boris_rozhin/227486","published_at":"2026-09-27T00:03:01Z","collected_at":"2026-09-27T01:52:23.097403Z","title":"","text":"⠀ 🔴 Интервью на фронте с добровольцами - участниками СВО. Наш Центр истории СВО (директор - М. С. Григорьев) продолжает сбор воспоминаний участников специальной военной операции в рамках проекта \"Хранить вечно\". Смотреть на Rutube Смотреть предыдущее интервью Часть 3 Часть 4. Доброволец с позывным \"Минай\", добровольческий отряд \"Буран\": 00:00 \"После мы на себе эвакуировали семь человек. Это был первый серьёзный случай. Мы вытащили его на себе и дотянули до укрепа в этой же лесополосе. Потом надо было доставить его до \"Подковы\" — это ещё порядка полутора-двух километров. 00:25 Там было много открытой местности. Из лесополосы выбегаешь — метров 600 открытого пространства, высокий подъём, метров 40. Порядка двух километров до более-менее безопасного места. За эту работу меня представили к нескольким наградам. 01:41 Ранение получил во время эвакуации раненого. Там находилась ещё одна группа из трёх штурмовиков. Они немного заблудились. Мы два-три дня ходили их искали. 02:37 Они получили ранения на той же \"Саге\". Подорвались на ПОМ-ках и были тяжело ранены. Остались в том же закрепе, где до этого находился ранее эвакуированный. Когда мы пришли за ними, нас обнаружили. Туда начали заходи","html":"","media":["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/fV_9LQDF3bO8QYIfefRl5Ww03yqCJ9mCRxxxwR1_zYcKYNmkii6ZoP4Q41ihywKi3kEmygikRAGoOP7KiBQ25DkvPvq9Zvdh2t_AasEoA8PWQlzNJtzQws8qNpO49gJyMtSFLtcN6nPXIi7wJsJPGu-S3nZwSzK2sdUiYLN7wrrViygJU7pv7tRrwPfnMG9ft_pmtIAS-I8mWZcJK47XSyEEDEYesK0Ns3RS6rH-vxg-TlvgRG8qtTxEvR4jB7wEKTef6yAydX61NlK5vtv708HKgt8wYsz2OOG1FJjLM03gLF7IcJQJRwnF0-4uG6mwMnilFKHd4Ludq5N5_n5TqA","https://rutube.ru/video/e96ca185125eb1e996bba77b4e872450/"],"author":"Boris Rozhin","language":"und","group":"ru-milbloggers","perspective